{% comment %}
  Cart drawer bundle widget — collapsed-by-default inline editor.

  The collapsed summary row uses the SAME structural classes as a
  regular cart line item (sections/theme__cart.liquid:1179-1419) so
  fonts, spacing, padding, and positions match exactly. Only the
  image area (3-stack instead of one image) and the trash slot
  (chevron toggle instead of trash) differ. A quantity stepper sits
  in the row's bottom slot and changes ALL THREE bundled line items
  in lockstep so adjusting it adds/removes whole bundles.

  Rendered once per bundle group inside the cart-drawer x-for loop.
  Wrapped in its own x-data scope so each bundle has independent
  selection / dropdown / open-collapse state.

  Reads from parent x-for scope:
    - item.__bundleGroup: array of the 3 line items sharing _bundle_id

  Inherits from cart drawer root Alpine scope:
    - changeCartItemQuantity(key, qty, openCart, refresh)
    - cart_loading

  Relies on (rendered once from sections/theme__cart.liquid):
    - snippets/bundle__cart-edit-data.liquid — produces the JSON data
      blob (id="bundle-cart-edit-data") AND the window.bundleCartEdit
      factory function used here by x-data.
{% endcomment %}

{%- assign _trash_icon_size = section.settings.trash_icon_size | default: 20 -%}

<div
  class="cart__bundle-group"
  :class="{ 'is-open': bundleOpen }"
  x-data="bundleCartEdit(item.__bundleGroup)"
  x-init="init(); _applyBundleDiscount()"
  @cart:updated.window="_applyBundleDiscount()"
  @keydown.escape.window="bundleOpen ? (dropdownOpen >= 0 ? dropdownOpen = -1 : bundleOpen = false) : null">

  {%- comment -%}
    Collapsed summary row — mirrors a regular cart line item exactly.
    Structure (matches sections/theme__cart.liquid:1179-1419):
      [image area] [details column: title+variant row, then qty+chevron row] [price column inside details]
    All Tailwind classes are copy-paste from the regular row so fonts,
    spacing, padding, and positions stay identical. The image area is
    the only visual departure (3-stack instead of a single image),
    plus the trash slot is replaced with the expand chevron.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div
    class="
      cart__bundle-summary-row cart__item-row border--b-width flex w-full p-4 gap-2
      {{ section.settings.main_color_scheme_first }}
      {{ section.settings.main_color_border }}
    ">

    {%- comment -%}
      Image area — matches the regular row's `w-[20%]` width container
      so the title column aligns identically. Inside, a 3-stack:
      wallet (large, top), lanyard + chapstick (smaller, side by side
      below). Image URLs piggyback on the `_240x240` / `_120x120` CDN
      size suffix the regular line already uses.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="cart__bundle-summary-imgcol w-[20%] h-full" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="cart__bundle-summary-stack">
        <div class="cart__bundle-summary-stack-main">
          <img
            class="cart__bundle-summary-img"
            :src="currentProduct(0).image ? currentProduct(0).image.replace(/\.(jpg|jpeg|png|webp|gif)(\?|$)/i, '_240x240.$1$2') : ''"
            :alt="currentProduct(0).title || ''"
            width="160"
            height="160"
            loading="eager"
            decoding="async" />
        </div>
        <div class="cart__bundle-summary-stack-row">
          <div class="cart__bundle-summary-stack-side">
            <img
              class="cart__bundle-summary-img"
              :src="currentProduct(1).image ? currentProduct(1).image.replace(/\.(jpg|jpeg|png|webp|gif)(\?|$)/i, '_120x120.$1$2') : ''"
              :alt="currentProduct(1).title || ''"
              width="80"
              height="80"
              loading="eager"
              decoding="async" />
          </div>
          <div class="cart__bundle-summary-stack-side">
            <img
              class="cart__bundle-summary-img"
              :src="currentProduct(2).image ? currentProduct(2).image.replace(/\.(jpg|jpeg|png|webp|gif)(\?|$)/i, '_120x120.$1$2') : ''"
              :alt="currentProduct(2).title || ''"
              width="80"
              height="80"
              loading="eager"
              decoding="async" />
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      Details column — copies the regular row's structure exactly:
      top sub-row holds the title block (left) + price column (right);
      bottom sub-row holds the qty stepper (left) + trash slot (right,
      now a chevron). Same Tailwind utility classes throughout.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="flex flex-col flex-grow animation-500"
      {% if settings.enable_animations %}
        :class="{ 'opacity-50' : cart_loading }"
      {% endif %}>
      <div class="flex gap-2 justify-between items-start">
        <div class="no-underline hover:no-underline type__nav">
          <p class="cart__item-title mb-0 !leading-tight !font-bold{% if item_title_token_class != '' %} {{ item_title_token_class }}{% endif %}">
            Trifecta Bundle
          </p>
          <p class="cart__item-variant mb-0 opacity-75 type--small{% if item_variant_token_class != '' %} {{ item_variant_token_class }}{% endif %}">
            Wallet &middot; Lanyard &middot; Chapstick
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="cart__item-prices flex flex-col items-end">
          <span
            class="cart__item-price !leading-tight{% if item_price_token_class != '' %} {{ item_price_token_class }}{% endif %}"
            x-text="formatMoney(bundleLineTotal())"></span>
          <span x-show="totals().savings > 0" x-cloak>
            <s
              class="cart__item-compare !leading-tight{% if item_compare_token_class != '' %} {{ item_compare_token_class }}{% endif %}"
              x-text="formatMoney(bundleLineSubtotal())"></s>
          </span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="flex flex-col gap-2 mt-2">
        <div class="flex gap-2 justify-between items-center pr-[14px]">
          {%- comment -%}
            Quantity stepper — clones the regular row's stepper markup
            and classes exactly. Increment / decrement adjust all
            three bundle line items in lockstep via setBundleQty().
            Decrementing past 1 removes the whole bundle (mirrors the
            regular row dropping to qty 0).
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="flex items-center gap-4 w-full min-w-0">
          <div
            class="cart__qty-stepper max-w-[150px] color__text color__border-divider-1 border--width hover:color__border-selected-1 border__input--radius relative flex w-full overflow-hidden">
            <button
              type="button"
              class="cart__qty-btn btn--smaller shrink-0 !rounded-none border--r-width color__border-divider-1"
              :disabled="bundleQtyLoading || loading"
              title="{{ 'cart.general.decrease' | t }}"
              @click.prevent.stop="bundleQty() <= 1 ? removeBundle() : setBundleQty(bundleQty() - 1)">
              {% render 'component__icon', icon: 'minus', size: '14', class: '' %}
            </button>
            <label class="sr-only" :for="'cart-bundle-' + (bundleId || 'qty')">
              {{- 'products.general.quantity' | t -}}
            </label>
            <input
              :id="'cart-bundle-' + (bundleId || 'qty')"
              type="text"
              inputmode="numeric"
              class="cart__qty-input form-input !border-0 text-center !rounded-none"
              :value="bundleQty()"
              @keydown.enter.prevent.stop="setBundleQty($event.target.value)"
              @change.debounce.stop="setBundleQty($event.target.value)" />
            <div
              class="btn__spinner btn--smaller !w-auto !color__bg-body"
              :class="{ '!visible color__bg-overlay-1 z-10' : bundleQtyLoading }">
              {% render 'component__icon', icon: 'spinner', size: '16', class: '' %}
            </div>
            <button
              type="button"
              class="cart__qty-btn btn--smaller shrink-0 !rounded-none border--l-width color__border-divider-1"
              :disabled="bundleQtyLoading || loading"
              title="{{ 'cart.general.increase' | t }}"
              @click.prevent.stop="setBundleQty(bundleQty() + 1)">
              {% render 'component__icon', icon: 'plus', size: '14', class: '' %}
            </button>
          </div>

          {%- comment -%}
            Edit/expand chevron sits just left of center, next to the
            quantity stepper (16px gap + padded hit area for thumbs,
            per merchant); the TRASH icon keeps the far-right slot
            matching the regular cart rows.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <button
            type="button"
            class="cart__bundle-summary-chevron-btn !p-2 -m-2 shrink-0 !bg-transparent !border-0"
            :aria-expanded="bundleOpen ? 'true' : 'false'"
            aria-controls="js:bundle-panel-{{ item.key | default: 'bundle' }}"
            aria-label="Edit bundle"
            title="Edit bundle"
            @click="bundleOpen = !bundleOpen">
            {% render 'component__icon', icon: 'edit', size: _trash_icon_size, class: '' %}
          </button>
          </div>

          <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
            <button
              type="button"
              class="cart__bundle-trash cart__trash-btn !py-0 !px-0 !bg-transparent !border-0"
              :class="{ 'btn--loading' : loading }"
              :disabled="loading"
              aria-label="Remove bundle"
              title="Remove bundle"
              @click="removeBundle()">
              {% render 'component__icon', icon: 'trash', size: _trash_icon_size, class: '' %}
            </button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    Collapsible editor panel — the existing 3-card editor renders
    verbatim. Wrapped in a CSS grid whose template-rows animates
    0fr ↔ 1fr; the inner clips overflow during the transition.
    :inert while collapsed pulls every interactive descendant out
    of the tab order without removing it from the DOM, so the editor
    state survives close → reopen.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div
    class="cart__bundle-collapse"
    id="js:bundle-panel-{{ item.key | default: 'bundle' }}">
    <div class="cart__bundle-collapse-inner" :inert="!bundleOpen">

      <ul class="cart__bundle-items" aria-label="Bundle items">
        <template x-for="(slot, sIdx) in slots" :key="sIdx">
          <li class="cart__bundle-item" :class="{ 'is-active-dropdown': dropdownOpen === sIdx }">
            <button
              type="button"
              class="cart__bundle-item-button"
              :disabled="loading"
              :aria-expanded="dropdownOpen === sIdx"
              @click="toggleDropdown(sIdx)">
              <div class="cart__bundle-item-img-wrap">
                <img
                  class="cart__bundle-item-img"
                  :src="currentProduct(sIdx).image ? currentProduct(sIdx).image.replace(/\.(jpg|jpeg|png|webp|gif)(\?|$)/i, '_240x240.$1$2') : ''"
                  :alt="currentProduct(sIdx).title || ''"
                  width="160"
                  height="160"
                  loading="eager"
                  decoding="async" />
              </div>
              <div class="cart__bundle-item-body">
                {%- if settings.trifecta_show_slot_label != false -%}
                <p class="cart__bundle-item-slot" x-text="slot.label"></p>
                {%- endif -%}
                {%- comment -%}
                  Title shows only the color part of the conventional
                  "<Color> - <Type>" name — same shortName() the dropdown
                  swatches use. The full type renders on its own line below
                  when the merchant has the toggle on. Mirrors the PDP card
                  layout 1:1 so the cart bundle reads the same.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                <p class="cart__bundle-item-title" x-text="shortName(currentProduct(sIdx).title || '')"></p>
                {%- if settings.trifecta_show_item_type != false -%}
                <p class="cart__bundle-item-type" x-text="currentProduct(sIdx).type || ''"></p>
                {%- endif -%}
                <p class="cart__bundle-item-price" x-text="formatMoney(currentProduct(sIdx).price || 0)"></p>
              </div>
              <span class="cart__bundle-item-change">
                <span x-text="dropdownOpen === sIdx ? 'Close' : 'Change'"></span>
                <span class="cart__bundle-item-caret" aria-hidden="true">▾</span>
              </span>
            </button>
            <button
              type="button"
              class="cart__bundle-item-remove"
              :disabled="loading"
              @click="removeSlot(sIdx)"
              :aria-label="'Remove ' + slot.label + ' from bundle'"
              title="Remove from bundle">
              <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="M3 3L11 11M11 3L3 11" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round"/>
              </svg>
            </button>
          </li>
        </template>
      </ul>

      {%- comment -%}
        Toolbar above the dropdown panel holds the filter pills (left,
        horizontally scrollable) and the close X (right) on one row —
        mirrors the PDP trifecta dropdown. The pills scroll under the X
        rather than overlapping it.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="cart__bundle-dropdown-toolbar" x-show="dropdownOpen >= 0" x-cloak>
        <div class="cart__bundle-type-tabs">
          <button
            type="button"
            class="cart__bundle-type-tab"
            :class="{ 'is-active': dropdownOpen >= 0 && selectedType[dropdownOpen] === '' }"
            @click="selectType(dropdownOpen, '')">
            <span>All</span>
          </button>
          <template x-for="type in (dropdownOpen >= 0 ? typesForSlot(dropdownOpen) : [])" :key="type">
            <button
              type="button"
              class="cart__bundle-type-tab"
              :class="{ 'is-active': dropdownOpen >= 0 && selectedType[dropdownOpen] === type }"
              @click="selectType(dropdownOpen, type)">
              <span x-text="type"></span>
            </button>
          </template>
        </div>
        <button
          type="button"
          class="cart__bundle-dropdown-close"
          aria-label="Close"
          @click="dropdownOpen = -1">✕</button>
      </div>

      <div
        class="cart__bundle-dropdown"
        :class="{ 'is-open': dropdownOpen >= 0 }">

        <div class="cart__bundle-swatches">
          <template x-for="p in (dropdownOpen >= 0 ? productsForCurrentType(dropdownOpen) : [])" :key="p.handle">
            <button
              type="button"
              class="cart__bundle-swatch"
              :class="{
                'is-selected': dropdownOpen >= 0 && currentProduct(dropdownOpen).handle === p.handle,
                'is-unavailable': !p.available
              }"
              :disabled="!p.available || loading"
              :aria-label="p.title + (p.available ? '' : ' (sold out)')"
              :title="p.title"
              @click="selectProduct(dropdownOpen, p)">
              <span class="cart__bundle-swatch-img">
                <img :src="p.image ? p.image.replace(/\.(jpg|jpeg|png|webp|gif)(\?|$)/i, '_120x120.$1$2') : ''" :alt="p.title" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
              </span>
              <span class="cart__bundle-swatch-name" x-text="shortName(p.title)"></span>
            </button>
          </template>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="cart__bundle-status cart__bundle-status--loading" x-show="loading" x-cloak>Updating bundle…</p>
      <p class="cart__bundle-status cart__bundle-status--error" x-show="error" x-text="error" x-cloak></p>

      {%- comment -%}
        The remove-bundle trash now lives on the collapsed summary row
        (right-edge slot, matching regular line items) — no duplicate
        trigger inside the expanded panel.
      {%- endcomment -%}

    </div>
  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    Scoped styles:
    1) Neutralize the legacy .cart__bundle-group padding from
       assets/bundle-builder.css so the new summary row inherits the
       regular .cart__item-row's own p-4 padding — that's what makes
       the bundle row align with the rows above and below it.
    2) Style the image stack (kept from the previous iteration — the
       merchant approved this look).
    3) Position the chevron in the trash slot at the regular-row's
       size and rotation behaviour.
    4) Collapse animation via grid-template-rows 0fr → 1fr; the inner
       wrapper holds the editor's horizontal padding so the cards
       align with the summary above.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <style>
    /* 1) Reset the legacy group container — summary + collapse each
          carry their own padding now. */
    .cart__bundle-group {
      padding: 0 !important;
      gap: 0 !important;
      display: block;
    }

    /* 2) Image stack inside the regular w-[20%] image column. */
    .cart__bundle-summary-imgcol { flex: 0 0 20%; }
    .cart__bundle-summary-stack {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-rows: 1fr auto;
      gap: 4px;
      width: 100%;
    }
    .cart__bundle-summary-stack-main {
      width: 100%;
      aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;
      border-radius: 6px;
      overflow: hidden;
      background: var(--color-bg-overlay-1, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.04));
    }
    .cart__bundle-summary-stack-row {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      gap: 4px;
    }
    .cart__bundle-summary-stack-side {
      width: 100%;
      aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;
      border-radius: 4px;
      overflow: hidden;
      background: var(--color-bg-overlay-1, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.04));
    }
    .cart__bundle-summary-img {
      width: 100%;
      height: 100%;
      object-fit: cover;
      display: block;
    }

    /* 3) Chevron in the regular row's trash slot. Matches the trash
          icon's size (merchant's trash_icon_size setting) and the
          regular row's right-edge inset (pr-[14px]). */
    .cart__bundle-summary-chevron-btn {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      cursor: pointer;
      color: inherit;
    }
    .cart__bundle-summary-chevron {
      display: inline-flex;
      transition: transform 0.2s ease;
    }
    .cart__bundle-summary-chevron.is-flipped {
      transform: rotate(180deg);
    }

    /* 4) Collapse: grid-template-rows 0fr → 1fr animates the child's
          auto height with no measurement step. The editor inside
          gets horizontal + bottom padding so its cards line up with
          the summary row's p-4 padding above. */
    .cart__bundle-collapse {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-rows: 0fr;
      transition: grid-template-rows 0.28s ease;
    }
    .cart__bundle-group.is-open .cart__bundle-collapse {
      grid-template-rows: 1fr;
    }
    .cart__bundle-collapse-inner {
      overflow: hidden;
      min-height: 0;
      padding: 12px 16px 16px;
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 12px;
    }
    .cart__bundle-group:not(.is-open) .cart__bundle-collapse-inner {
      padding-top: 0;
      padding-bottom: 0;
    }
  </style>
</div>
